AndroidManifest:
    Required Permissions:
        <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO" />
            Required for recording audio
        <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
            Required for sending data to Firebase
        <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" />
            Required for Location Services

Firebase Setup:
    This was setup on a Free Tier of Firebase.
    The best way to configure this for you Firebase Instance is to follow
        Android Studio's Firebase Setup Instructions (Tools -> Firebase -> Firestore)
    You will need your own google-services.json file and any additional configuration as required.
    Firebase Authentication is configured as Anonymous. If user tracking is required,
        then this will need to be modified.


On / Off toggling via Firebase is currently unimplemented.
    This can be done via Firebase Cloud Messaging, but was not pursued
        because framework for recording and processing was prioritized.

